{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLRbSSMRcmUHHMbVhpDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RRg36hHsjapVVa9PZf5XN6","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","path":"packages/esm-service-queues-app","since":"2026-04-16","perPage":20,"page":2},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4149,"cache_read_input_tokens":18620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4149},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc27e77d-f0b3-4d01-878e-78974a732dcf","uuid":"b6419e60-7503-4127-851a-18adcbf6fd1d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:23:45.612Z","request_id":"req_011CgLRbSCEGCFexeswa8sjc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RRg36hHsjapVVa9PZf5XN6":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","path":"packages/esm-service-queues-app","since":"2026-04-16","perPage":20,"page":2}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RRg36hHsjapVVa9PZf5XN6","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RRg36hHsjapVVa9PZf5XN6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c2d4b9fc2937b12a5dcf09d55d509c3a4abfac77\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T23:35:08+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty (#2766)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Unbold the metric tile header labels\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Match the header label style used in the other metrics strip\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T20:54:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\\n\\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\\nwere lost.\\n\\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\\nactions, reusing the queue table's action menu items so the handlers, labels\\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\\n\\nCarbon's OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\\n\\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\\n\\nPlace the card's actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\\n\\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d6ca1f1c04e431bcaa7c79d46fd9027639db49eb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:04:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#2764)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore: Adopt the shared Prettier configuration\\n\\nUse @openmrs/prettier-config in the existing config wrapper and pin Prettier to 3.9.8. Keep our bracketSameLine override.\\n\\n* Apply Prettier 3.9.8 formatting\\n\\nApply the measured indentation change in the service queues config schema. Leave existing formatting issues elsewhere untouched.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c741c18000e41edbaefa3266b184c26507835735\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T16:31:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2760)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4f6944cc87106a2c5a59558189084d1dde29c2f2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T16:33:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2755)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d9cbd2742a8d8842f6c7ae4d243254f195c06bd7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T22:12:04+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name (#2750)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name\\n\\nThe queue page's metric tile takes its label from the queue status concept\\n(\\\"In Service\\\"), while the card list above the tables used a fixed\\n\\\"Attending\\\" string, so the two disagreed. Derive the card heading, its error\\nstate title, and the clinic overview's column and totals card from the\\nconfigured defaultTransitionStatus concept instead, falling back to\\n\\\"In Service\\\" until the concept loads.\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/attending-patients/attending-patients.test.tsx\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1f4098170806704451ed195a9922dc1a30ebcedc\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T20:01:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5958: Default the queue location to the one selected in Service Queues (#2731)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(service-queues): ensure queueLocation defaults to sessionLocation asynchronously\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Mutagubya Jonathan\",\"authorEmail\":\"mutajonathan4@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2824b5ebeda2fb6f7f6f47bf0db6dcf7dc47007d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-15T00:33:12+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5967: Show the queue number instead of the status in the default queue table (#2738)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9a3d0e504d8371af43aa703a2b374ed5c505a035\",\"date\":\"2026-09-13T16:31:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2745)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2d6a9eafd1b35cacf22cef9a774fd836cb8fa622\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T16:30:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2739)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"324414d0c72d04ca6272e401180b9e0a9d1b847a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T15:52:58+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5770: Add a Clinic Administrator screen for Service Queues (#2681)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5770: Add a Clinic Administrator screen for Service Queues\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5770: Read clinic metrics from the queue module\\n\\nRolls the clinic metrics up server-side via groupBy=queue, rather than fetching\\nevery unfinished queue entry at a location and reducing them in the browser.\\nRequires openmrs/openmrs-module-queue#123; reverting this commit drops that\\ndependency.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Address review feedback on the clinic administrator screen\\n\\n- Show '--' in the totals cards when the roll-up request failed, not only\\n  while it is loading.\\n- Only mount the selected tab's content. Carbon keeps hidden panels mounted,\\n  so the tab nobody was looking at kept polling for queue entries.\\n- Show \\\"No status configured\\\" only for a queue that allows no status at all.\\n  One allowing just the in-service status has no table, but the Attending\\n  cards above it are its list.\\n- Gate the add-a-patient control on `defaultStatusConceptUuid`, the status a\\n  new entry actually starts in, so a status-scoped table only offers it where\\n  the patient would land. The unscoped waiting list keeps it either way: it is\\n  the dashboard's own add action.\\n- Drop `totalWaitMinutes` from the roll-up fixtures. It is not a field the\\n  hook returns; annotating rather than casting the fixture flags the next one.\\n- Cover what the tests were assuming: that `queueUuid` scopes the Attending\\n  cards and the status table to that queue, that `sortRow` compares longest\\n  waits numerically and keeps queues with no wait at the bottom either way,\\n  and that the unselected tab stays unmounted.\\n- Correct the comment on the allowed-status order: it comes from the concept\\n  set in the dictionary, not from the backend reversing it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Scope the clinic wait metrics to waiting entries\\n\\nThe queue module ends an entry and starts a new one at transition, so an\\nIn Service entry's startedAt is when service began rather than when the\\npatient joined the queue. Asking for the open-wait metrics over every\\nunfinished entry therefore reported time in service as waiting time.\\n\\nSplit the roll-up into two requests: the counts still cover every\\nunfinished entry, so Waiting and Attending are unchanged, while the wait\\nmetrics are scoped to the waiting status. The wait request leaves out\\nqueues with nobody waiting, so the counts decide which rows exist.\\n\\nAlso notes the dependency on queue module #123 in the config schema,\\ndrops the duplicate \\\"Queues\\\" heading from the overview's error state,\\nand gives the error and loading cards the table's inline spacing.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Read the clinic metrics in a single request\\n\\nThe queue module grew a `waitStatus` parameter that scopes the open-wait\\nmetrics server-side while leaving the counts over every unfinished entry,\\nso the counts and the two wait figures can come from one request rather\\nthan two.\\n\\nThat halves the requests -- each loaded every unfinished entry at the\\nlocation on the server -- measures the counts and the waits at one\\ninstant, and deletes the join by queue UUID.\\n\\nIt also drops the \\\"leaves out queues with nobody waiting\\\" premise: the\\nbackend seeds a row for every queue at the location, so a queue nobody is\\nwaiting in comes back with a null wait rather than being absent.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Address review feedback on the empty state and imports\\n\\n`EmptyState` now carries the border and padding every caller was passing it,\\nso the tile styles itself and a caller only names what differs. Attending\\npatients and the clinic overview drop their override entirely, the queue\\nscreen keeps just its margin, and the admin page keeps the two deltas that\\nmake it sit flush beneath a table.\\n\\nAlso rename the attending-patients test and move the clinic overview's hook\\nimport below the components, both as suggested in review.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Name the queue module version the clinic screen needs\\n\\nQueue module #123 is merged, so the config description names 3.1.0 rather\\nthan linking the pull request. routes.json already requires `queue\\n>=3.1.0-0 <4.0.0`, added for queue-entry-metrics, so the floor it declares\\nand the one #123 needs are the same version.\\n\\nThe admin page's two empty states also stop repeating the same className:\\nthe inset that sits the tile flush beneath a table is set once, on the\\nsection holding it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Report a retired queue rather than blanking the page\\n\\nThe queue list leaves out retired queues, but the clinic overview's rows\\ncome from the queue entries, which do not, so a retired queue somebody is\\nstill waiting in is reachable by link. `useQueue` resolves such a uuid to\\nnothing without erroring, so it slipped past the `errorFetchingQueue`\\nguard and the view read `.uuid` off it, blanking the page. The existing\\n\\\"Invalid Queue\\\" notification now covers that case too.\\n\\nThe loading branch becomes an early return, so the guard narrows\\n`selectedQueue` for the rest of the body rather than the component leaning\\non reasoning the compiler cannot follow. That also retires a nested\\nternary and the optional chaining on a value now known to be there.\\n\\nAlso drop `QueueTableTabConfig`, dead since the queue-table-by-status\\ncomponent went, and trim a comment and a test that restated what they sit\\nnext to.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Gate the clinic overview on the privilege alone\\n\\n* (test) O3-5770: Select the waiting list tab in the queue e2e specs\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Mark retired queues on the clinic overview and harden the privilege gate\\n\\nA retired queue that still holds open entries now shows its name with a\\nRetired tag instead of a link, since the queue list leaves retired queues\\nout and the link landed on \\\"Invalid Queue\\\". The Queue type gains the\\noptional `retired` flag the grouped metric response carries.\\n\\nAn empty `clinicAdministratorScreen.privilege` now hides the tabs rather\\nthan opening them to everyone, because userHasAccess grants access to every\\nuser when the privilege is falsy.\\n\\nThe metric tiles show a skeleton while the clinic figures load, and the\\nconfig description drops the module version sentence that routes.json\\nalready declares.\\n\\nThe e2e spec asserts the clinic overview tab and its queues table before\\nopening the waiting list. Tests cover the retired row, the empty privilege,\\nthe privilege passed to userHasAccess, and the loading state.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a861402d9b82c74f158bbc1cfc9078029b2b7002\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T16:32:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2737)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"923bd8e1466edabca16a2340acaf4b441a8346ff\",\"date\":\"2026-09-08T16:33:25-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2732)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-08T20:40:11+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don't submit a prefilled service before the entries load\\n\\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\\npatient's queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\\n\\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\\n\\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \\\"Invalid Submission\\\" message\\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\\nmatching the message alone.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\\n\\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \\\"already in every queue\\\"\\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\\n\\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\\nnever once returned a cached value.\\n\\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\\n\\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\\n  \\\"already in this queue\\\" surface instead of a generic message.\\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d74f8ad97ef7f4e01747398265ac8777f4604ccf\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T14:27:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve queue screen empty state contrast\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Wrap the queue screen empty state in a contextual Carbon layer so its tile uses the white layer background instead of blending into the grey page, matching the attending empty state. Cover the layer in the existing empty state test.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8b8da99d381ac4e0cb2435990b9df02c83b1dd1c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T11:40:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Align empty state text styles with the styleguide empty card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Use the $text-02 variable instead of the --cds-text-secondary token for the attending and queue screen empty state text, and add the bottom margin the styleguide's empty card content has. The resolved colour is unchanged; the margin is the only visible difference.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c2bbf83ffd29c2573ff70349c5343dc62afa501d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T17:12:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2712)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"dbf505e0ef8b17d54e198a35e87b32f974e4121e\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T09:53:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2709)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"38b8d47fc6a86a5dd706c6cff4e25313b7defeac\",\"date\":\"2026-08-31T12:31:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve attending empty state contrast (#2707)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Wrap the attending empty state in a contextual Carbon layer so its tile uses the white layer background. Clarify the empty-state message and cover the resulting layer and copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":95}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc27e77d-f0b3-4d01-878e-78974a732dcf","uuid":"42a716ee-719a-47c7-85b3-18cfcae7c104","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:23:45.732Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c2d4b9fc2937b12a5dcf09d55d509c3a4abfac77\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T23:35:08+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty (#2766)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Unbold the metric tile header labels\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Match the header label style used in the other metrics strip\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T20:54:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\\n\\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\\nwere lost.\\n\\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\\nactions, reusing the queue table's action menu items so the handlers, labels\\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\\n\\nCarbon's OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\\n\\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\\n\\nPlace the card's actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\\n\\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d6ca1f1c04e431bcaa7c79d46fd9027639db49eb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:04:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#2764)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore: Adopt the shared Prettier configuration\\n\\nUse @openmrs/prettier-config in the existing config wrapper and pin Prettier to 3.9.8. Keep our bracketSameLine override.\\n\\n* Apply Prettier 3.9.8 formatting\\n\\nApply the measured indentation change in the service queues config schema. Leave existing formatting issues elsewhere untouched.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c741c18000e41edbaefa3266b184c26507835735\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T16:31:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2760)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4f6944cc87106a2c5a59558189084d1dde29c2f2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T16:33:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2755)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d9cbd2742a8d8842f6c7ae4d243254f195c06bd7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T22:12:04+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name (#2750)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name\\n\\nThe queue page's metric tile takes its label from the queue status concept\\n(\\\"In Service\\\"), while the card list above the tables used a fixed\\n\\\"Attending\\\" string, so the two disagreed. Derive the card heading, its error\\nstate title, and the clinic overview's column and totals card from the\\nconfigured defaultTransitionStatus concept instead, falling back to\\n\\\"In Service\\\" until the concept loads.\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/attending-patients/attending-patients.test.tsx\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1f4098170806704451ed195a9922dc1a30ebcedc\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T20:01:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5958: Default the queue location to the one selected in Service Queues (#2731)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(service-queues): ensure queueLocation defaults to sessionLocation asynchronously\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Mutagubya Jonathan\",\"authorEmail\":\"mutajonathan4@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2824b5ebeda2fb6f7f6f47bf0db6dcf7dc47007d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-15T00:33:12+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5967: Show the queue number instead of the status in the default queue table (#2738)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9a3d0e504d8371af43aa703a2b374ed5c505a035\",\"date\":\"2026-09-13T16:31:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2745)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2d6a9eafd1b35cacf22cef9a774fd836cb8fa622\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T16:30:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2739)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"324414d0c72d04ca6272e401180b9e0a9d1b847a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T15:52:58+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5770: Add a Clinic Administrator screen for Service Queues (#2681)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5770: Add a Clinic Administrator screen for Service Queues\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5770: Read clinic metrics from the queue module\\n\\nRolls the clinic metrics up server-side via groupBy=queue, rather than fetching\\nevery unfinished queue entry at a location and reducing them in the browser.\\nRequires openmrs/openmrs-module-queue#123; reverting this commit drops that\\ndependency.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Address review feedback on the clinic administrator screen\\n\\n- Show '--' in the totals cards when the roll-up request failed, not only\\n  while it is loading.\\n- Only mount the selected tab's content. Carbon keeps hidden panels mounted,\\n  so the tab nobody was looking at kept polling for queue entries.\\n- Show \\\"No status configured\\\" only for a queue that allows no status at all.\\n  One allowing just the in-service status has no table, but the Attending\\n  cards above it are its list.\\n- Gate the add-a-patient control on `defaultStatusConceptUuid`, the status a\\n  new entry actually starts in, so a status-scoped table only offers it where\\n  the patient would land. The unscoped waiting list keeps it either way: it is\\n  the dashboard's own add action.\\n- Drop `totalWaitMinutes` from the roll-up fixtures. It is not a field the\\n  hook returns; annotating rather than casting the fixture flags the next one.\\n- Cover what the tests were assuming: that `queueUuid` scopes the Attending\\n  cards and the status table to that queue, that `sortRow` compares longest\\n  waits numerically and keeps queues with no wait at the bottom either way,\\n  and that the unselected tab stays unmounted.\\n- Correct the comment on the allowed-status order: it comes from the concept\\n  set in the dictionary, not from the backend reversing it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Scope the clinic wait metrics to waiting entries\\n\\nThe queue module ends an entry and starts a new one at transition, so an\\nIn Service entry's startedAt is when service began rather than when the\\npatient joined the queue. Asking for the open-wait metrics over every\\nunfinished entry therefore reported time in service as waiting time.\\n\\nSplit the roll-up into two requests: the counts still cover every\\nunfinished entry, so Waiting and Attending are unchanged, while the wait\\nmetrics are scoped to the waiting status. The wait request leaves out\\nqueues with nobody waiting, so the counts decide which rows exist.\\n\\nAlso notes the dependency on queue module #123 in the config schema,\\ndrops the duplicate \\\"Queues\\\" heading from the overview's error state,\\nand gives the error and loading cards the table's inline spacing.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Read the clinic metrics in a single request\\n\\nThe queue module grew a `waitStatus` parameter that scopes the open-wait\\nmetrics server-side while leaving the counts over every unfinished entry,\\nso the counts and the two wait figures can come from one request rather\\nthan two.\\n\\nThat halves the requests -- each loaded every unfinished entry at the\\nlocation on the server -- measures the counts and the waits at one\\ninstant, and deletes the join by queue UUID.\\n\\nIt also drops the \\\"leaves out queues with nobody waiting\\\" premise: the\\nbackend seeds a row for every queue at the location, so a queue nobody is\\nwaiting in comes back with a null wait rather than being absent.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Address review feedback on the empty state and imports\\n\\n`EmptyState` now carries the border and padding every caller was passing it,\\nso the tile styles itself and a caller only names what differs. Attending\\npatients and the clinic overview drop their override entirely, the queue\\nscreen keeps just its margin, and the admin page keeps the two deltas that\\nmake it sit flush beneath a table.\\n\\nAlso rename the attending-patients test and move the clinic overview's hook\\nimport below the components, both as suggested in review.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Name the queue module version the clinic screen needs\\n\\nQueue module #123 is merged, so the config description names 3.1.0 rather\\nthan linking the pull request. routes.json already requires `queue\\n>=3.1.0-0 <4.0.0`, added for queue-entry-metrics, so the floor it declares\\nand the one #123 needs are the same version.\\n\\nThe admin page's two empty states also stop repeating the same className:\\nthe inset that sits the tile flush beneath a table is set once, on the\\nsection holding it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Report a retired queue rather than blanking the page\\n\\nThe queue list leaves out retired queues, but the clinic overview's rows\\ncome from the queue entries, which do not, so a retired queue somebody is\\nstill waiting in is reachable by link. `useQueue` resolves such a uuid to\\nnothing without erroring, so it slipped past the `errorFetchingQueue`\\nguard and the view read `.uuid` off it, blanking the page. The existing\\n\\\"Invalid Queue\\\" notification now covers that case too.\\n\\nThe loading branch becomes an early return, so the guard narrows\\n`selectedQueue` for the rest of the body rather than the component leaning\\non reasoning the compiler cannot follow. That also retires a nested\\nternary and the optional chaining on a value now known to be there.\\n\\nAlso drop `QueueTableTabConfig`, dead since the queue-table-by-status\\ncomponent went, and trim a comment and a test that restated what they sit\\nnext to.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Gate the clinic overview on the privilege alone\\n\\n* (test) O3-5770: Select the waiting list tab in the queue e2e specs\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5770: Mark retired queues on the clinic overview and harden the privilege gate\\n\\nA retired queue that still holds open entries now shows its name with a\\nRetired tag instead of a link, since the queue list leaves retired queues\\nout and the link landed on \\\"Invalid Queue\\\". The Queue type gains the\\noptional `retired` flag the grouped metric response carries.\\n\\nAn empty `clinicAdministratorScreen.privilege` now hides the tabs rather\\nthan opening them to everyone, because userHasAccess grants access to every\\nuser when the privilege is falsy.\\n\\nThe metric tiles show a skeleton while the clinic figures load, and the\\nconfig description drops the module version sentence that routes.json\\nalready declares.\\n\\nThe e2e spec asserts the clinic overview tab and its queues table before\\nopening the waiting list. Tests cover the retired row, the empty privilege,\\nthe privilege passed to userHasAccess, and the loading state.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a861402d9b82c74f158bbc1cfc9078029b2b7002\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T16:32:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2737)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"923bd8e1466edabca16a2340acaf4b441a8346ff\",\"date\":\"2026-09-08T16:33:25-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2732)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-08T20:40:11+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don't submit a prefilled service before the entries load\\n\\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\\npatient's queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\\n\\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\\n\\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \\\"Invalid Submission\\\" message\\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\\nmatching the message alone.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\\n\\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \\\"already in every queue\\\"\\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\\n\\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\\nnever once returned a cached value.\\n\\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\\n\\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\\n  \\\"already in this queue\\\" surface instead of a generic message.\\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d74f8ad97ef7f4e01747398265ac8777f4604ccf\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T14:27:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve queue screen empty state contrast\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Wrap the queue screen empty state in a contextual Carbon layer so its tile uses the white layer background instead of blending into the grey page, matching the attending empty state. Cover the layer in the existing empty state test.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8b8da99d381ac4e0cb2435990b9df02c83b1dd1c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T11:40:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Align empty state text styles with the styleguide empty card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Use the $text-02 variable instead of the --cds-text-secondary token for the attending and queue screen empty state text, and add the bottom margin the styleguide's empty card content has. The resolved colour is unchanged; the margin is the only visible difference.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c2bbf83ffd29c2573ff70349c5343dc62afa501d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T17:12:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2712)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"dbf505e0ef8b17d54e198a35e87b32f974e4121e\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T09:53:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2709)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"38b8d47fc6a86a5dd706c6cff4e25313b7defeac\",\"date\":\"2026-08-31T12:31:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve attending empty state contrast (#2707)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Wrap the attending empty state in a contextual Carbon layer so its tile uses the white layer background. Clarify the empty-state message and cover the resulting layer and copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":95}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RRg36hHsjapVVa9PZf5XN6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLRbSSMRcmUHHMbVhpDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X5qxrwFgHYqf9UuRzQaLpK","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","path":"packages/esm-service-queues-app","since":"2026-04-16","perPage":20,"page":3},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4149,"cache_read_input_tokens":18620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4149},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc27e77d-f0b3-4d01-878e-78974a732dcf","uuid":"c72c6ce3-d4b8-4305-b971-69c707e36b4d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:23:46.059Z","request_id":"req_011CgLRbSCEGCFexeswa8sjc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X5qxrwFgHYqf9UuRzQaLpK":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","path":"packages/esm-service-queues-app","since":"2026-04-16","perPage":20,"page":3}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X5qxrwFgHYqf9UuRzQaLpK","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X5qxrwFgHYqf9UuRzQaLpK","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b46bb56449a768d9ffb652006aa5eea2a8960c08\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:08:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2705)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f4163794c31570904d1b77259cfadd135136fb91\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T22:58:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#2704)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7212897e35ee9efa79192770f019651dcbd66cc1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:42:34+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views (#2600)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on unified visit summary\\n\\n* (fix) Restore visit note authoring on the Current visit tab\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix obs group crash, encounter editing and expanded row styles\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix the e2e specs covering the unified visit summary\\n\\nServe the patient notes app in the e2e frontend, scope the encounter assertions\\nto the expanded row's table, and revalidate queue entries once per submit rather\\nthan twice.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Analyze the e2e database before running the specs\\n\\nThe seeded image reports zero rows for every table, so MariaDB plans the queue\\nentry query, whose join spans ~44 tables, from full scans. That is harmless while\\nqueue_entry is empty and takes minutes once a spec inserts a row, hanging\\nservice-queues.spec.ts. Analyzing the schema takes under a second.\\n\\nAlso adds the mutate mock that usePastVisits now returns to the PastVisit tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on the unified visit summary\\n\\nMoves the queue spec's API setup into e2e/commands so other queue specs can reuse\\nit, guards its teardown against a partial setup, and scopes the encounter locator\\nto the table. Also guards the edit handler against an unresolved patient, restores\\nthe date validity check, widens the form entry window to match the chart, and\\ncovers the past visit filter and the slot state in tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Hand the visit summary our mutate for encounter deletes\\n\\nDeleting an encounter opens a modal rather than a workspace, so the workspace\\nsubscription never fires and both tabs kept showing the deleted encounter.\\nPairs with the chart accepting mutateVisitContext alongside onEditEncounter.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Wait for the patient before mounting the vitals extension\\n\\nThe vitals extension reads  during render — with a nonzero\\nbmiMinimumAge, shouldShowBmi reaches patient.birthDate before the extension's\\nown loading guard — so mounting it while usePatient is still resolving throws\\ninto the error boundary. Extends the existing patient-loading test to cover it.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5763: Drop the CI database statistics workaround\\n\\nThe queue entry list was slow because the module fetched its associations\\neagerly, not because of the image. Fixed properly in openmrs-module-queue#122,\\nso this step comes out.\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5763: Hand the patient down to the visit summary extension\\n\\nThe shared visit summary reads the patient from the chart store, which Service\\nQueues never populates, so its embedded form view had nothing to render with.\\nBoth tabs now pass `patient` in the slot state, and the slot assertions cover\\n`patient`, `onEditEncounter` and `mutateVisitContext` so dropping one is caught\\nhere rather than in the e2e run.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f72aa14ce03ec28258c0acbe4507ac100b6fe8db\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T19:33:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2703)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7a2ccf502f6f557aa2628dee2371b2e70f8be5e3\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T18:52:46+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design (#2615)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design\\n\\n* (fix) e2e tests\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n- Bound the average wait time to entries started today and render '--'\\n  instead of 'NaN mins' when the backend has no completed waits to average\\n- Surface loading and error states in the Attending section so a failed\\n  request is no longer indistinguishable from nobody being attended\\n- Cap the Attending cards at three behind a 'View all' toggle and say\\n  'No one is being attended' explicitly when the list is empty\\n- Exclude Cancelled/Completed/Missed appointments from the expected\\n  appointments count and tab\\n- Translate appointment statuses, use a single interpolated key for the\\n  waiting list tab label, and use the framework age() helper so infants\\n  no longer render as '0 years old'\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Address second round of review feedback on queues dashboard\\n\\nAdds concepts.waitingStatusConceptUuid so the waiting list, its tab count and\\nthe \\\"Waiting\\\" metric stop overloading defaultStatusConceptUuid, which only\\ndescribes the status a newly created queue entry starts in. All three read the\\nnew config, so the count cannot disagree with the rows beneath it.\\n\\n- Count the waiting list via queue-entry-metrics instead of paging through\\n  every entry. useQueueEntriesMetrics now reports isLoading and error so the\\n  tab label shows no momentary \\\"(0)\\\" before the request settles.\\n- Drop useServiceMetricsCount: it hardcoded status=Waiting as a concept name\\n  and has no remaining callers.\\n- Send forDate as an ISO 8601 string. The appointments module's DateUtil does\\n  not parse a ZZ numeric offset. The test now asserts the value, not the path.\\n- Show the selected service in the header even when the location is \\\"All\\\",\\n  since the modal permits that combination, and reset the service when the\\n  default location resolves, as services are scoped to a location.\\n- Look the expected-appointments name cell up through an id/patientUuid map\\n  rather than scanning every row on each render.\\n- Guard the service sort against a missing display, order attending-patients\\n  imports components before hooks, and drop an unused @carbon/type import.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Trim the waitingStatusConceptUuid description\\n\\nIts contrast with defaultStatusConceptUuid belongs in review, not in the\\nconfig reference that implementers read.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Scope the wait-time metric and Call action to the waiting status\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Remove the appointments features from the dashboard\\n\\nThe Expected appointments tab and Appointments today card only match\\nappointments whose location equals the selected queue location exactly,\\nand the alternative leaks other locations' appointments. Dropping both\\nuntil location tagging is settled.\\n\\nAlso formats Avg. wait time like the Wait time column, and shows --\\nwhen the backend has nothing to average.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Round the average wait time before guarding on it\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the wait-time window as UTC\\n\\nThe queue module parses startedOnOrAfter with a zone-less\\nSimpleDateFormat, so browser-local midnight was read in the server's\\ntimezone and hid everything queued before the client's offset elapsed.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Restructure the Attending card details\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Move the service and priority into a card footer\\n\\nSeparates them from the demographics with a rule, service left and pill\\nright, per design review. The card element is now the link itself rather\\nthan a wrapper around one.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Count the entries a search leaves in the waiting list heading\\n\\n`totalCount` is the server's count of every waiting entry, so the heading kept\\nreporting the full list while the table showed only the search results.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the metrics window as an unambiguous instant\\n\\nThe queue module could not parse a timezone offset, so browser-local midnight\\nwas being converted to UTC and sent zone-less — correct only because servers\\nusually run in UTC. openmrs-module-queue now parses REST date parameters with\\nConversionUtil, so send an ISO-8601 instant and let the server resolve it.\\n\\nRequires queue module 3.1.0 or later.\\n\\n* (chore) Require queue module 3.1.0 for queue-entry-metrics\\n\\nThe average wait time card sends `startedOnOrAfter` as an ISO-8601 instant,\\nwhich only queue 3.1.0 onwards parses, so declare that in the backend\\ndependencies instead of noting it in a code comment. The `-0` prerelease\\nfloor keeps SNAPSHOT builds valid for testing.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f2021aec08a29c7380aa08f74ac8af32cb27ca68\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T17:14:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2700)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2005c4e5e0b75fd20bc6ef97477dff378ea47cfa\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T21:07:26+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5765: Remove manual clear queue entries button (#2632)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8738f2fd169e6901c17079d0e5d318e7d2ea7508\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T16:33:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2677)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88a3958024123fe1223a94c91af0675f34d621f8\",\"date\":\"2026-08-10T23:11:53+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#2664)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\\n\\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing the root .eslintrc, the five\\npackage-level .eslintrc files, and .eslintignore. The seven ESLint plugin\\ndev dependencies the shared config provides are dropped, eslint moves from\\nthe end-of-life 8.57 line to ^9.39.0, and the --ext flag goes away since flat\\nconfig makes it redundant.\\n\\nRules this repo enforces beyond the shared defaults are kept in overlays:\\neqeqeq, the three ban-types successors that typescript-eslint's recommended\\npreset enables and the shared config turns off, and\\nreact-hooks/exhaustive-deps as a warning. Five packages enforced\\nno-explicit-any through their own .eslintrc, which ESLint 9 would ignore,\\nso that is now a path-scoped overlay covering the same five. Comparing the\\neffective rule set before and after on the same file, nothing this repo\\nenforced is lost, and both configurations report no findings over the same\\n680 files.\\n\\nThere are four kinds of fallout from the plugin versions the shared config\\npins.\\n\\neslint-plugin-react-hooks moves from 4.6 to 7.1, which recognizes React's\\nuse() hook. Playwright fixtures receive a callback named use and call it,\\nso the rule reports every fixture. rules-of-hooks is therefore off for\\ne2e, where React hook rules have no meaning.\\n\\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1 to 2.11. Eleven specs had a\\ntrailing top-level test.afterEach, which now warns. A top-level hook\\napplies to every test in the file wherever it sits, so moving it above the\\ntests changes nothing at runtime. Three page.selectOption calls become\\nlocator calls, which Playwright's own types point to as the replacement.\\nThe blank-line changes are autofixes.\\n\\nSeventeen eslint-disable comments in e2e/commands/encounter-operations.ts\\nnamed playwright rules. The playwright preset only applies to\\ne2e/**/*.spec.ts, so those comments never suppressed anything, and in flat\\nconfig a comment naming an unregistered rule is a hard error.\\n\\nTwo testing-library directives go away. The one in a test file is no longer\\nneeded, since that plugin moves from 6.5 to 7.16 and no longer reports\\nthere. The one in tools/test-utils.tsx named a rule that never applied to\\nit, since the preset only covers *.test.{ts,tsx}, so it is the same dead\\ncomment case as above.\\n\\n* (chore) Remove redundant cross-env wrappers\\n\\nThe lint scripts do not set environment variables, so they can invoke ESLint directly. Remove the unused root dependency and refresh the lockfile.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4ab45c348ea730a9138c03bd72f7d01de93e3006\",\"date\":\"2026-08-08T16:31:20-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2662)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b4fa6bf0cb6141b90b1737507868ebe222cf9bba\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:50:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2660)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1af0d22714f5c85e3da513226acdb89d11bd1ac7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T16:52:53-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9a9bd207717ecc2e1f551cafcc389cc1fa8ea40c\",\"date\":\"2026-08-03T16:49:49-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2653)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ef2db8daa43241206aa85622ee9bf304928919bc\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:47:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2650)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3ebf29fd6a764a0b353cc7377b6a58ddcb9a3543\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:52:31+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5681: Queue-screen widget polls regardless of user activity (#2564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2a05d2f532ff2713513d91ed56aafde26957a27e\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:11:14+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one (#2611)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one\\n\\n* (feat) Rename move confirmation strings and add status/priority tests\\n\\n* (fix) Keep the legacy transition action working\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on the combined move action\\n\\n- Use neutral \\\"Queue entry updated\\\" copy for the submit notifications, since\\n  the modal now covers queue, status, and priority changes.\\n- Don't repeat a button action in the overflow menu when a deprecated action\\n  resolves to one already declared as a button (buttons: ['move'] with\\n  overflowMenu: ['transition'] rendered Move twice).\\n- Assert that the new priority reaches transitionQueueEntry in the\\n  priority-only test.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41835e897a10a266922a55adeb668632f52c90df\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T01:55:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove nested anchor from the Service Queues admin card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The card wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor that carried the href.\\nClickableTile renders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested\\nanchors and a dead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link,\\nthen land on the tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did\\nnothing on Enter.\\n\\nThe href now lives on ClickableTile directly, matching how other admin\\ncards such as the Form Builder card are implemented. The cardLink\\nwrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no outer anchor left\\nto reset.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6315a9e5daf6d52ab2bda68f70a8f931e6a7b91\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T16:47:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\\n\\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\\n\\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\\n  already scopes results to today\\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\\n\\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\\nmatch the actual scope.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\\n\\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\\n\\n* (chore) translation changes\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\\n\\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \\\"with an active visit\\\", but\\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"171573ddff7840281d76268628e2684ed3be64d0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-29T18:47:10+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5693: Trim queue entry representation to what the table renders (#2583)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":95}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc27e77d-f0b3-4d01-878e-78974a732dcf","uuid":"4d616d88-d9df-498d-992c-35b841eb4bf1","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:23:46.116Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b46bb56449a768d9ffb652006aa5eea2a8960c08\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:08:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2705)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f4163794c31570904d1b77259cfadd135136fb91\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T22:58:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#2704)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7212897e35ee9efa79192770f019651dcbd66cc1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:42:34+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views (#2600)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on unified visit summary\\n\\n* (fix) Restore visit note authoring on the Current visit tab\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix obs group crash, encounter editing and expanded row styles\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix the e2e specs covering the unified visit summary\\n\\nServe the patient notes app in the e2e frontend, scope the encounter assertions\\nto the expanded row's table, and revalidate queue entries once per submit rather\\nthan twice.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Analyze the e2e database before running the specs\\n\\nThe seeded image reports zero rows for every table, so MariaDB plans the queue\\nentry query, whose join spans ~44 tables, from full scans. That is harmless while\\nqueue_entry is empty and takes minutes once a spec inserts a row, hanging\\nservice-queues.spec.ts. Analyzing the schema takes under a second.\\n\\nAlso adds the mutate mock that usePastVisits now returns to the PastVisit tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on the unified visit summary\\n\\nMoves the queue spec's API setup into e2e/commands so other queue specs can reuse\\nit, guards its teardown against a partial setup, and scopes the encounter locator\\nto the table. Also guards the edit handler against an unresolved patient, restores\\nthe date validity check, widens the form entry window to match the chart, and\\ncovers the past visit filter and the slot state in tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Hand the visit summary our mutate for encounter deletes\\n\\nDeleting an encounter opens a modal rather than a workspace, so the workspace\\nsubscription never fires and both tabs kept showing the deleted encounter.\\nPairs with the chart accepting mutateVisitContext alongside onEditEncounter.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Wait for the patient before mounting the vitals extension\\n\\nThe vitals extension reads  during render — with a nonzero\\nbmiMinimumAge, shouldShowBmi reaches patient.birthDate before the extension's\\nown loading guard — so mounting it while usePatient is still resolving throws\\ninto the error boundary. Extends the existing patient-loading test to cover it.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5763: Drop the CI database statistics workaround\\n\\nThe queue entry list was slow because the module fetched its associations\\neagerly, not because of the image. Fixed properly in openmrs-module-queue#122,\\nso this step comes out.\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5763: Hand the patient down to the visit summary extension\\n\\nThe shared visit summary reads the patient from the chart store, which Service\\nQueues never populates, so its embedded form view had nothing to render with.\\nBoth tabs now pass `patient` in the slot state, and the slot assertions cover\\n`patient`, `onEditEncounter` and `mutateVisitContext` so dropping one is caught\\nhere rather than in the e2e run.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f72aa14ce03ec28258c0acbe4507ac100b6fe8db\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T19:33:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2703)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7a2ccf502f6f557aa2628dee2371b2e70f8be5e3\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T18:52:46+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design (#2615)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design\\n\\n* (fix) e2e tests\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n- Bound the average wait time to entries started today and render '--'\\n  instead of 'NaN mins' when the backend has no completed waits to average\\n- Surface loading and error states in the Attending section so a failed\\n  request is no longer indistinguishable from nobody being attended\\n- Cap the Attending cards at three behind a 'View all' toggle and say\\n  'No one is being attended' explicitly when the list is empty\\n- Exclude Cancelled/Completed/Missed appointments from the expected\\n  appointments count and tab\\n- Translate appointment statuses, use a single interpolated key for the\\n  waiting list tab label, and use the framework age() helper so infants\\n  no longer render as '0 years old'\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Address second round of review feedback on queues dashboard\\n\\nAdds concepts.waitingStatusConceptUuid so the waiting list, its tab count and\\nthe \\\"Waiting\\\" metric stop overloading defaultStatusConceptUuid, which only\\ndescribes the status a newly created queue entry starts in. All three read the\\nnew config, so the count cannot disagree with the rows beneath it.\\n\\n- Count the waiting list via queue-entry-metrics instead of paging through\\n  every entry. useQueueEntriesMetrics now reports isLoading and error so the\\n  tab label shows no momentary \\\"(0)\\\" before the request settles.\\n- Drop useServiceMetricsCount: it hardcoded status=Waiting as a concept name\\n  and has no remaining callers.\\n- Send forDate as an ISO 8601 string. The appointments module's DateUtil does\\n  not parse a ZZ numeric offset. The test now asserts the value, not the path.\\n- Show the selected service in the header even when the location is \\\"All\\\",\\n  since the modal permits that combination, and reset the service when the\\n  default location resolves, as services are scoped to a location.\\n- Look the expected-appointments name cell up through an id/patientUuid map\\n  rather than scanning every row on each render.\\n- Guard the service sort against a missing display, order attending-patients\\n  imports components before hooks, and drop an unused @carbon/type import.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Trim the waitingStatusConceptUuid description\\n\\nIts contrast with defaultStatusConceptUuid belongs in review, not in the\\nconfig reference that implementers read.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Scope the wait-time metric and Call action to the waiting status\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Remove the appointments features from the dashboard\\n\\nThe Expected appointments tab and Appointments today card only match\\nappointments whose location equals the selected queue location exactly,\\nand the alternative leaks other locations' appointments. Dropping both\\nuntil location tagging is settled.\\n\\nAlso formats Avg. wait time like the Wait time column, and shows --\\nwhen the backend has nothing to average.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Round the average wait time before guarding on it\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the wait-time window as UTC\\n\\nThe queue module parses startedOnOrAfter with a zone-less\\nSimpleDateFormat, so browser-local midnight was read in the server's\\ntimezone and hid everything queued before the client's offset elapsed.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Restructure the Attending card details\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Move the service and priority into a card footer\\n\\nSeparates them from the demographics with a rule, service left and pill\\nright, per design review. The card element is now the link itself rather\\nthan a wrapper around one.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Count the entries a search leaves in the waiting list heading\\n\\n`totalCount` is the server's count of every waiting entry, so the heading kept\\nreporting the full list while the table showed only the search results.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the metrics window as an unambiguous instant\\n\\nThe queue module could not parse a timezone offset, so browser-local midnight\\nwas being converted to UTC and sent zone-less — correct only because servers\\nusually run in UTC. openmrs-module-queue now parses REST date parameters with\\nConversionUtil, so send an ISO-8601 instant and let the server resolve it.\\n\\nRequires queue module 3.1.0 or later.\\n\\n* (chore) Require queue module 3.1.0 for queue-entry-metrics\\n\\nThe average wait time card sends `startedOnOrAfter` as an ISO-8601 instant,\\nwhich only queue 3.1.0 onwards parses, so declare that in the backend\\ndependencies instead of noting it in a code comment. The `-0` prerelease\\nfloor keeps SNAPSHOT builds valid for testing.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f2021aec08a29c7380aa08f74ac8af32cb27ca68\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T17:14:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2700)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2005c4e5e0b75fd20bc6ef97477dff378ea47cfa\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T21:07:26+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5765: Remove manual clear queue entries button (#2632)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8738f2fd169e6901c17079d0e5d318e7d2ea7508\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T16:33:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2677)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88a3958024123fe1223a94c91af0675f34d621f8\",\"date\":\"2026-08-10T23:11:53+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#2664)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\\n\\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing the root .eslintrc, the five\\npackage-level .eslintrc files, and .eslintignore. The seven ESLint plugin\\ndev dependencies the shared config provides are dropped, eslint moves from\\nthe end-of-life 8.57 line to ^9.39.0, and the --ext flag goes away since flat\\nconfig makes it redundant.\\n\\nRules this repo enforces beyond the shared defaults are kept in overlays:\\neqeqeq, the three ban-types successors that typescript-eslint's recommended\\npreset enables and the shared config turns off, and\\nreact-hooks/exhaustive-deps as a warning. Five packages enforced\\nno-explicit-any through their own .eslintrc, which ESLint 9 would ignore,\\nso that is now a path-scoped overlay covering the same five. Comparing the\\neffective rule set before and after on the same file, nothing this repo\\nenforced is lost, and both configurations report no findings over the same\\n680 files.\\n\\nThere are four kinds of fallout from the plugin versions the shared config\\npins.\\n\\neslint-plugin-react-hooks moves from 4.6 to 7.1, which recognizes React's\\nuse() hook. Playwright fixtures receive a callback named use and call it,\\nso the rule reports every fixture. rules-of-hooks is therefore off for\\ne2e, where React hook rules have no meaning.\\n\\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1 to 2.11. Eleven specs had a\\ntrailing top-level test.afterEach, which now warns. A top-level hook\\napplies to every test in the file wherever it sits, so moving it above the\\ntests changes nothing at runtime. Three page.selectOption calls become\\nlocator calls, which Playwright's own types point to as the replacement.\\nThe blank-line changes are autofixes.\\n\\nSeventeen eslint-disable comments in e2e/commands/encounter-operations.ts\\nnamed playwright rules. The playwright preset only applies to\\ne2e/**/*.spec.ts, so those comments never suppressed anything, and in flat\\nconfig a comment naming an unregistered rule is a hard error.\\n\\nTwo testing-library directives go away. The one in a test file is no longer\\nneeded, since that plugin moves from 6.5 to 7.16 and no longer reports\\nthere. The one in tools/test-utils.tsx named a rule that never applied to\\nit, since the preset only covers *.test.{ts,tsx}, so it is the same dead\\ncomment case as above.\\n\\n* (chore) Remove redundant cross-env wrappers\\n\\nThe lint scripts do not set environment variables, so they can invoke ESLint directly. Remove the unused root dependency and refresh the lockfile.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4ab45c348ea730a9138c03bd72f7d01de93e3006\",\"date\":\"2026-08-08T16:31:20-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2662)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b4fa6bf0cb6141b90b1737507868ebe222cf9bba\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:50:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2660)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1af0d22714f5c85e3da513226acdb89d11bd1ac7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T16:52:53-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9a9bd207717ecc2e1f551cafcc389cc1fa8ea40c\",\"date\":\"2026-08-03T16:49:49-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2653)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ef2db8daa43241206aa85622ee9bf304928919bc\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:47:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2650)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3ebf29fd6a764a0b353cc7377b6a58ddcb9a3543\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:52:31+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5681: Queue-screen widget polls regardless of user activity (#2564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2a05d2f532ff2713513d91ed56aafde26957a27e\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:11:14+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one (#2611)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one\\n\\n* (feat) Rename move confirmation strings and add status/priority tests\\n\\n* (fix) Keep the legacy transition action working\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on the combined move action\\n\\n- Use neutral \\\"Queue entry updated\\\" copy for the submit notifications, since\\n  the modal now covers queue, status, and priority changes.\\n- Don't repeat a button action in the overflow menu when a deprecated action\\n  resolves to one already declared as a button (buttons: ['move'] with\\n  overflowMenu: ['transition'] rendered Move twice).\\n- Assert that the new priority reaches transitionQueueEntry in the\\n  priority-only test.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41835e897a10a266922a55adeb668632f52c90df\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T01:55:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove nested anchor from the Service Queues admin card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The card wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor that carried the href.\\nClickableTile renders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested\\nanchors and a dead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link,\\nthen land on the tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did\\nnothing on Enter.\\n\\nThe href now lives on ClickableTile directly, matching how other admin\\ncards such as the Form Builder card are implemented. The cardLink\\nwrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no outer anchor left\\nto reset.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6315a9e5daf6d52ab2bda68f70a8f931e6a7b91\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T16:47:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\\n\\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\\n\\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\\n  already scopes results to today\\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\\n\\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\\nmatch the actual scope.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\\n\\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\\n\\n* (chore) translation changes\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\\n\\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \\\"with an active visit\\\", but\\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi